# Diwali 2026: Immersive 3D Celebration Experience
## Project Vision

Create an exceptional, fully immersive one-page Diwali 2026 celebration experience using modern web technologies and a breathtaking ultra-realistic 3D environment.

This should not feel like a conventional festival website, portfolio, landing page, or collection of cards.

The goal is to create a majestic, cinematic, interactive 3D world inspired by the epic return of **Lord Rama to Ayodhya** after defeating Ravana — transformed into a polished digital Diwali 2026 celebration. The core centerpiece is the **majestic moment of Lord Rama releasing the divine fire arrow (Agni Astra) from his celestial bow to defeat Ravana**, followed by the triumphant return to Ayodhya where the entire kingdom is lit with millions of diyas — the origin of Diwali itself.

The visitor should feel as if they have stepped inside the Ramayana — witnessing the battle, the victory, and the glorious homecoming.

The experience should combine:
- Ultra-realistic 3D environment design (high-fidelity, detailed mesh, smooth geometry)
- Royal Indian epic aesthetics (Ayodhya kingdom, ancient architecture)
- Ramayana-inspired storytelling
- Majestic stylized characters (Rama, Ravana, Sita, Lakshmana, Hanuman)
- Interactive divine objects (fire bow, celestial arrows, pushpak vimana)
- Smooth cinematic camera movement
- Scroll-driven epic storytelling
- Festival decorations (diyas, rangoli, fireworks, torans)
- Subtle particle effects (fire embers, sparks, golden dust, fireworks)
- Beautiful dramatic lighting (fire-lit, golden, divine glow)
- Ambient animation
- Micro-interactions
- Cinematic transitions
- Responsive design

The final result should feel **majestic, divine, triumphant, cinematic, artistic, and technologically breathtaking**.

