## 28. Responsive Design

Mobile must be treated as a first-class experience.

On mobile:
- Reduce polygon complexity
- Reduce particle count
- Simplify distant objects
- Reduce dynamic lighting
- Reduce expensive post-processing
- Simplify camera paths
- Disable complex pointer interactions
- Replace hover with tap
- Preserve the core storytelling

**The mobile version should still feel like an epic 3D Diwali experience.**

---

## 29. Performance

The website is 3D and animation-heavy, so performance is critical.

Implement:
- GLTF/GLB model optimization (with ultra-detail preserved)
- Texture compression (KTX2, basis)
- Lazy loading
- Progressive scene loading
- Instanced meshes (for diyas, flowers, etc.)
- Efficient particle systems
- GPU-friendly transforms
- Efficient React rendering
- Proper Three.js cleanup
- Proper GSAP cleanup
- Responsive rendering quality
- Device-aware quality settings
- Reduced shadow complexity on weaker devices
- Avoid unnecessary post-processing
- Avoid excessive transparent materials
- Avoid excessive dynamic lights
- Provide a lightweight fallback for lower-end devices

**Ultra-detailed models must be optimized without losing visual quality.**

